# Shape analyses and loop fusion, written in A0 (DESIGN.md 7a): the port of src/optimize.ts
# lines 716-1343 (storeOnly, overwritesState, fillRun, lazyArms, producerShape, fuseLoops) and of
# `borrowLive` of src/core.ts. The wasm emitter (compiler/emit_wasm.a0) does not `use` this file:
# compiler/boot.a0 runs it between the optimizer and the emitter, and the emitter reads the
# results from the SHAPE TABLE, one table `sh` (u32x128x200) that is an extra input of its chunk.
#
# Inputs: the OPTIMIZED chunk tables of compiler/emit_wasm.a0: types u32x384x65, tlist u32x128x65,
# fns u32x128x45 (7 words: 0 body flag, 1 parameter count, 2 first tlist word, 3 result type, 4
# first node, 5 node count, 6 packed ret; word 6 is 0 for a function without a body), nodes
# u32x128x128 (6 words a node: 0, op, operand count, first operand, callee, pred), args
# u32x128x512 (operand pairs), ntys u32x128x24 (node types). A node's index in its function is its
# position; the global node index g of node j is (first node of the function) + j. Type indices
# 0 1 2 are u32 bool io; an aggregate has an index of 3 or more.
#
# THE SHAPE TABLE (columns of 2816 words indexed by global node index g, function columns of 1024):
#   FILL  0      fold node: the fillRun trip count (> 0) or 0. The body is the node's callee, the
#                stored value operand 2 of the callee's ret `set` node, the fill's nodes all callee
#                nodes except that ret node, in order.
#   OWN   2816   lazyArms: the position (in its function) + 1 of the select a node is private to,
#                else 0
#   ARM   5632   1 / 2: the node belongs to the select's first / second arm (arm lists: the nodes
#                with OWN = that select, in node order)
#   OVER  8448   fold node: overwritesState 0 / 1
#   BORR  11264  set / put node (target operand 0) and fold / loop node (state operand 1) of an
#                aggregate type whose target operand is a parameter or a node defined by
#                arr rec set put: borrowLive(fn, that operand, j, selfRead) with selfRead set for
#                set / put, else 0. Every other node is 0: only these are queried (the rest of
#                mutableHere is the emitter's).
#   FUSED 14080  function column: 1 + the function that is the fused form of this function, else 0
#   SYN   15104  function column: 1 a synthetic fused body (never emitted by itself, only
#                inlined), 2 a fused function
#   MISS  16128  the count n, then n chunk function indices (16129..) whose rows have no body
#                (fns word 6 = 0) and whose body an analysis needed: end the chunk with code 7 and
#                these indices (the emitter appends its own requests to its own list)
#   TIO   17152  type column (8320 types): 1 when the type contains an io token
#   25472..      scalars: node, operand pair, function, type and tlist counts (used by fusion)
#
# Calls (pure; the shape table is threaded through folds as state). Tables: ty tl fns nodes args
# nt in the order of compiler/emit_wasm.a0 `wachunk` (types, tlist, fns, nodes, args, ntys).
#   shinit ty tl nty -> sh
#       the table with only TIO filled
#   shcounts sh nn na nf nty ntl -> sh
#       the free positions of the OPTIMIZED chunk tables (nodes, operand pairs, functions, types,
#       tlist words), kept in the scalars: fusion appends there (the optimizer leaves holes, so
#       these are the ends of the used regions, including its next free operand)
#   shpass sh ty tl fns nodes args nt f -> sh
#       FILL OWN ARM OVER BORR (and MISS) of function f; run it for every function that has a body
#       and may be emitted or inlined
#
# Loop fusion (src/optimize.ts fuseLoops with recordState, 8 rounds), per function f, stateless:
# the tables of the chunk stay as they are; the fused view is a modified COPY of them.
#   shfcheck ty tl fns nodes args nt sh f rs -> (found, missing)
#       cheap: is there a fusion site in f (rs: recordState, true for wasm), or the chunk function
#       whose body is needed and absent (4294967295 for none): call shfuse only when found
#   shfuse ty tl fns nodes args nt sh f rs -> (status, missing, nf1, ty, tl, fns, nodes, nt)
#   shfargs ty tl fns nodes args nt sh f rs -> args
#       the fused view in the tables' layout (two calls because one A0 value is at most 65536
#       words): function f is replaced IN PLACE (its rows, nodes and operands are overwritten, or
#       appended at the end when the fused body is larger), and each fusion appends a synthetic
#       function (fns rows nf0 .. nf1 - 1, nf0 = the nf given to shcounts: parameters at the
#       end of tlist, nodes and operands after the counts; fns word 0 = 1 + 2 literalIterations)
#       and, for a recurrence, its (state, previous element) record type. The synthetic bodies
#       are optimized with ozopt1 (compiler/optimize.a0), as src/optimize.ts finishBody does.
#       status 0 nothing fuses (the tables are f as it was), 1 fused, 4 a table is full (the
#       capacities of one chunk: 2730 nodes, 32768 operand pairs, 822 functions, 8320 types and
#       tlist words: the driver must leave headroom, about 64 nodes and 1024 pairs a fused
#       function plus the size of f when its body grows), 7 a body is needed (missing).
#   shfsh sh ty tl fns nodes args nt f nf0 nf1 -> sh
#       with the fused tables: shpass of f and of every synthetic function, SYN[f] = 2, SYN[g] = 1
#       for g in nf0 .. nf1 - 1, FUSED[f] = f + 1
# The emitter emits f from the fused view; if its code then calls a function with SYN = 1 out of
# line (a synthetic body that was not inlined: src/optimize.ts emitFused) it emits f from the
# original tables instead. Synthetic functions are never emitted by themselves.
#
use "optimize.a0"

@zarr zsh u32x128x200 200
@zarr zcol u32x128x24 24
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Types: which type indices contain an io token (column TIO of the shape table, 17152 + type)

fn shtiof u32 u32 u32x128x200 u32x128x65 u32 -> u32
i add p4 p1
@rd f p3 i
fi add f 17152
@rd t p2 fi
r or p0 t
ret r
end
fn shtios u32x128x200 u32 u32x384x65 u32x128x65 -> u32x128x200
@ty tag p2 p1 0
@ty ta p2 p1 1
@ty tb p2 p1 2
isio eq p1 2
isarr eq tag 4
isrec eq tag 5
eidx select isarr tb 0
ei add eidx 17152
@rd ev p0 ei
ev1 select isarr ev 0
nf select isrec tb 0
f0 fold shtiof nf 0 p0 p3 ta
r1 select isio 1 0
a1 or r1 ev1
b1 or a1 f0
ix add p1 17152
@wr w p0 ix b1
ret w
end
# the shape table of a chunk with p2 types: only the io column is filled (shinit); the node
# columns are written by shpass
fn shinit u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32 -> u32x128x200
z call zsh
r fold shtios p2 z p0 p1
ret r
end
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# storeOnly (src/optimize.ts): the ret node of function p3 when it is `set p0 p1 v` and p0 is
# otherwise unused, else 4294967295

# operand k of a node (args first p3): is it p0 where it is not the target of the set at jr?
fn shsoa u32 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 -> u32
s add p3 p1
@aw kd p2 s 0
@aw vl p2 s 1
@isop isp kd vl 2 0
jj eq p4 p5
kk eq p1 0
tg and jj kk
b1 select tg false isp
b select b1 1 0
r or p0 b
ret r
end
fn shsoj u32 u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32 u32 -> u32
g add p4 p1
@nwd na p2 g 2
@nwd af p2 g 3
r fold shsoa na p0 p3 af p1 p5
ret r
end
fn shstore u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x45 u32 -> u32
@fwd fst p2 p3 4
@fwd nfn p2 p3 5
@fwd rw p2 p3 6
retk shr rw 28
retv and rw 268435455
isn eq retk 1
jr select isn retv 0
g add fst jr
@nwd op p0 g 1
@nwd af p0 g 3
@aw k0 p1 af 0
@aw v0 p1 af 1
af1 add af 1
@aw k1 p1 af1 0
@aw v1 p1 af1 1
isset eq op 26
@isop a0ok k0 v0 2 0
@isop a1ok k1 v1 2 1
c1 and isn isset
c2 and a0ok a1ok
good and c1 c2
bad fold shsoj nfn 0 p0 p1 fst jr
nobad eq bad 0
ok and good nobad
r select ok jr 4294967295
ret r
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# producerShape / guardedPrevReads of body p3. Result: the guarded previous-element reads
# (word j of the column is 1 for body node j), the status (0 undefined, 1 a producer with
# previous-element reads (a recurrence), 2 a pure producer), 1 when guardedPrevReads is defined,
# 1 when the ret node is `set p0 p1 v`, and the ret node.

# operand k of node ju (first node p4): is the use of its node operand bad (not a select in
# the allowed arm of a zero test of the counter)? Marks the used node in the column.
fn shpb1 u32x128x24 u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32 u32 -> u32x128x24
gu add p4 p5
@nwd opu p2 gu 1
@nwd af p2 gu 3
s add af p1
@aw ak p3 s 0
@aw av p3 s 1
@aw c0k p3 af 0
@aw c0v p3 af 1
gd add p4 c0v
@nwd dop p2 gd 1
@nwd daf p2 gd 3
daf1 add daf 1
@aw xk p3 daf 0
@aw xv p3 daf 1
@aw yk p3 daf1 0
@aw yv p3 daf1 1
@isop xp xk xv 2 1
@isop x0 xk xv 3 0
@isop yp yk yv 2 1
@isop y0 yk yv 3 0
za and xp y0
zb and yp x0
zt0 or za zb
c0n eq c0k 1
iseq eq dop 12
isne eq dop 13
isel eq opu 18
k2 eq p1 2
k1 eq p1 1
e1 and iseq zt0
n1 and isne zt0
e2 and k2 e1
n2 and k1 n1
v1 or e2 n2
v2 and c0n v1
ok and isel v2
isnode eq ak 1
bad1 select ok false isnode
b select bad1 1 0
widx select isnode av 3071
@rd old p0 widx
nw or old b
@wr r p0 widx nw
ret r
end
fn shpb2 u32x128x24 u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32 -> u32x128x24
g add p4 p1
@nwd na p2 g 2
r fold shpb1 na p0 p2 p3 p4 p1
ret r
end
# node j (first node p4): a guarded previous-element read? State (prev column, failed, count).
fn shpb3 (u32x128x24,u32,u32) u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32x128x24 -> (u32x128x24,u32,u32)
prev at p0 0
fail at p0 1
cnt at p0 2
g add p4 p1
@nwd op p2 g 1
@nwd af p2 g 3
@aw k0 p3 af 0
@aw v0 p3 af 1
af1 add af 1
@aw k1 p3 af1 0
@aw v1 p3 af1 1
isget eq op 25
@isop a0p k0 v0 2 0
@isop a1c k1 v1 2 1
isg0 and isget a0p
nc select a1c false isg0
cand mov nc
isnode eq k1 1
d select isnode v1 0
gd add p4 d
@nwd dop p2 gd 1
@nwd daf p2 gd 3
daf1 add daf 1
@aw xk p3 daf 0
@aw xv p3 daf 1
@aw yk p3 daf1 0
@aw yv p3 daf1 1
@isop xp xk xv 2 1
@isop yp yk yv 2 1
@isop y1 yk yv 3 1
@isop yf yk yv 3 4294967295
@isop xf xk xv 3 4294967295
isub eq dop 3
iadd eq dop 2
sa and xp y1
sb and xp yf
sc and yp xf
sbc or sb sc
s1 and isub sa
s2 and iadd sbc
isprev or s1 s2
retn1 eq p5 1
retn2 eq p6 p1
retn and retn1 retn2
@rd bu p7 p1
bu0 eq bu 0
nr select retn false true
p1a and isnode isprev
p1b and p1a nr
p1c and p1b bu0
okp mov p1c
pv select cand okp false
f1 select cand okp true
failnow select f1 0 1
npv select pv 1 0
@wr prev2 prev p1 npv
cnt2 add cnt npv
fail2 or fail failnow
r rec prev2 fail2 cnt2
ret r
end
# operand k of node j (first node p4, args first p3): p0 used other than as a set target or by a
# previous-element read? State: failed.
fn shpb4a u32 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x24 u32 u32 -> u32
s add p3 p1
@aw ak p2 s 0
@aw av p2 s 1
@isop isp0 ak av 2 0
k0 eq p1 0
isset eq p5 p6
@rd pv p4 p5
ispv eq pv 1
okn or isset ispv
good and k0 okn
bad1 select good false isp0
b select bad1 1 0
r or p0 b
ret r
end
fn shpb4 u32 u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x24 u32 -> u32
g add p4 p1
@nwd na p2 g 2
@nwd af p2 g 3
r fold shpb4a na p0 p3 af p5 p1 p6
ret r
end
fn shprod u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x45 u32 bool -> (u32x128x24,u32,u32,u32,u32)
@fwd fst p2 p3 4
@fwd nfn p2 p3 5
@fwd rw p2 p3 6
retk shr rw 28
retv and rw 268435455
z call zcol
nfg select p4 nfn 0
badu fold shpb2 nfg z p0 p1 fst
s0 rec z 0 0
s1 fold shpb3 nfg s0 p0 p1 fst retk retv badu
prev at s1 0
gfail at s1 1
cnt at s1 2
isn eq retk 1
setj select isn retv 0
gs add fst setj
@nwd op p0 gs 1
@nwd af p0 gs 3
@aw k0 p1 af 0
@aw v0 p1 af 1
af1 add af 1
@aw k1 p1 af1 0
@aw v1 p1 af1 1
isset eq op 26
@isop a0ok k0 v0 2 0
@isop a1ok k1 v1 2 1
c1 and isn isset
c2 and a0ok a1ok
sok and c1 c2
f4 fold shpb4 nfg 0 p0 p1 fst prev setj
nf4 eq f4 0
ng eq gfail 0
o1 and sok nf4
okall and o1 ng
pure eq cnt 0
st0 select pure 2 1
st select okall st0 0
gdef select ng 1 0
sokv select sok 1 0
r rec prev st gdef sokv setj
ret r
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# fillRun and overwritesState of the fold node at global index p6 (tables: nodes args fns
# types tlist ntys). Result (count, missing): count the fill's trip count (0 for none; 1 or 0
# for overwritesState), missing the index of a callee whose body the answer needs and the chunk
# does not hold (4294967295 for none).

# operand k of a body node: scalar parameters only (p0 flag, k, args, af, tl, pf, shift)
fn shfa u32 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x65 u32 bool -> u32
s add p3 p1
@aw ak p2 s 0
@aw av p2 s 1
isb eq ak 4
isp eq ak 2
pi add p5 av
@rd pt p4 pi
pu eq pt 0
ige1 ge av 1
sc and ige1 pu
nsc select sc false true
pbad and isp nsc
k1 eq p1 1
isl eq ak 3
ige2 ge av 2
sc2 and ige2 sc
iu or isl sc2
uni mov iu
nuni select uni false true
sh1 and p6 k1
shbad and sh1 nuni
bad1 or isb pbad
bad2 or bad1 shbad
b select bad2 1 0
r or p0 b
ret r
end
fn shfb u32 u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x65 u32x128x24 u32 u32 u32 -> u32
# p0 bad, p1 j, nodes, args, tl, nt, fst, jr, pf
g add p6 p1
@nwd op p2 g 1
@nwd na p2 g 2
@nwd af p2 g 3
@rd nty p5 g
ge2 ge op 2
le9 le op 9
lane and ge2 le9
nl select lane false true
nu ne nty 0
nb1 or nl nu
isj eq p1 p7
nj select isj false true
shift ge op 8
sft and shift lane
ab fold shfa na 0 p3 af p4 p8 sft
nab ne ab 0
nb2 or nb1 nab
nb and nj nb2
b select nb 1 0
r or p0 b
ret r
end
fn shfill u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x45 u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x24 u32 -> (u32,u32)
@nwd op p0 p6 1
@nwd c p0 p6 4
@nwd af p0 p6 3
@aw ck p1 af 0
@aw cv p1 af 1
@rd tt p5 p6
@ty tag p3 tt 0
@ty tlen p3 tt 1
@ty telem p3 tt 2
isfold eq op 20
isarr eq tag 4
eu eq telem 0
ck3 eq ck 3
nz ne cv 0
lel le cv tlen
q1 and isfold isarr
q2 and q1 eu
q3 and q2 ck3
q4 and q3 nz
pre and q4 lel
@fwd rw p2 c 6
opaque eq rw 0
pop and pre opaque
miss select pop c 4294967295
@fwd fst2 p2 c 4
@fwd nfn2 p2 c 5
@fwd pf p2 c 2
jr call shstore p0 p1 p2 c
hasset ne jr 4294967295
jrs select hasset jr 0
bad fold shfb nfn2 0 p0 p1 p4 p5 fst2 jrs pf
gs add fst2 jrs
@nwd sa p0 gs 3
s2 add sa 2
@aw vk p1 s2 0
@aw vv p1 s2 1
vb eq vk 4
visp eq vk 2
vpi add pf vv
@rd vpt p4 vpi
vpu eq vpt 0
vge ge vv 1
vsc and vge vpu
nvsc select vsc false true
vpb and visp nvsc
vbad or vb vpb
nvbad select vbad false true
nopq select opaque false true
g1 and pre nopq
g2 and g1 hasset
nb eq bad 0
g3 and g2 nb
ok and g3 nvbad
count select ok cv 0
r rec count miss
ret r
end
fn shover u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x45 u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x24 u32 -> (u32,u32)
@nwd op p0 p6 1
@nwd c p0 p6 4
@nwd af p0 p6 3
@aw ck p1 af 0
@aw cv p1 af 1
@rd tt p5 p6
@ty tag p3 tt 0
@ty tlen p3 tt 1
isfold eq op 20
isarr eq tag 4
ck3 eq ck 3
gel ge cv tlen
q1 and isfold isarr
q2 and q1 ck3
pre and q2 gel
@fwd rw p2 c 6
opaque eq rw 0
pop and pre opaque
miss select pop c 4294967295
pr call shprod p0 p1 p2 c true
st at pr 1
hs ne st 0
nopq select opaque false true
o1 and pre nopq
o2 and o1 hs
count select o2 1 0
r rec count miss
ret r
end
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# borrowLive (src/core.ts) of the aggregate operand (p6 p7) of the node jq = p8 of the function
# with first node p4, ret (p5 = kind, p9 = value): 1 when some borrow of it is read at or after
# the node (at the node itself only when p10 is 0), or returned.

# node j: a borrow of the operand? State (borrows column, any)
fn shbp1 (u32x128x24,u32) u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32 u32 u32 -> (u32x128x24,u32)
bor at p0 0
any at p0 1
g add p5 p1
@nwd op p2 g 1
@nwd af p2 g 3
@rd nty p4 g
@aw k0 p3 af 0
@aw v0 p3 af 1
af1 add af 1
@aw k1 p3 af1 0
@aw v1 p3 af1 1
af2 add af 2
@aw k2 p3 af2 0
@aw v2 p3 af2 1
nonprim ge nty 3
@isop s0 k0 v0 p6 p7
n0 eq k0 1
@rd bv0 bor v0
b0 eq bv0 1
t0 and n0 b0
f0 or s0 t0
@isop s1 k1 v1 p6 p7
n1 eq k1 1
@rd bv1 bor v1
b1 eq bv1 1
t1 and n1 b1
f1 or s1 t1
@isop s2 k2 v2 p6 p7
n2 eq k2 1
@rd bv2 bor v2
b2 eq bv2 1
t2 and n2 b2
f2 or s2 t2
isget eq op 25
isat eq op 27
ismov eq op 1
issel eq op 18
ga or isget isat
gm or ga ismov
d0 and gm f0
f12 or f1 f2
d1 and issel f12
d2 or d0 d1
d3 and nonprim d2
nb select d3 1 0
@wr bor2 bor p1 nb
any2 or any nb
r rec bor2 any2
ret r
end
# use after: node j reads a borrow (inner step: operand k)
fn shbp2a u32 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x24 -> u32
s add p3 p1
@aw ak p2 s 0
@aw av p2 s 1
isn eq ak 1
@rd bv p4 av
b eq bv 1
u and isn b
x select u 1 0
r or p0 x
ret r
end
fn shbp2 u32 u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x24 u32 u32 -> u32
# p0 found, p1 j, nodes, args, fst, bor, jq, selfRead
gt gt p1 p6
eqj eq p1 p6
ns eq p7 0
e1 and eqj ns
act or gt e1
g add p4 p1
@nwd na p2 g 2
@nwd af p2 g 3
n select act na 0
r fold shbp2a n p0 p3 af p5
ret r
end
fn shborr u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32
# nodes args nt nfn fst retk ok ov jq retv selfRead
z call zcol
s0 rec z 0
s1 fold shbp1 p3 s0 p0 p1 p2 p4 p6 p7
bor at s1 0
any at s1 1
isn eq p5 1
@rd rb bor p9
rbb eq rb 1
rr and isn rbb
anyb ne any 0
n select anyb p3 0
f fold shbp2 n 0 p0 p1 p4 bor p8 p10
nf ne f 0
u or rr nf
r2 and anyb u
r select r2 1 0
ret r
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# lazyArms (src/optimize.ts). Per-function columns: UC the number of operand uses of node j
# among the nodes, EFF effectful (isEffectful) nodes.

fn shuck u32x128x24 u32 u32x128x512 u32 -> u32x128x24
s add p3 p1
@aw ak p2 s 0
@aw av p2 s 1
isn eq ak 1
widx select isn av 3071
@rd old p0 widx
inc select isn 1 0
nw add old inc
@wr r p0 widx nw
ret r
end
fn shucj u32x128x24 u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32 -> u32x128x24
g add p4 p1
@nwd na p2 g 2
@nwd af p2 g 3
r fold shuck na p0 p3 af
ret r
end
# effectful: operand k of node j (p0 flag, k, args, af, nt, fst, tl, pf, sh)
fn shefa u32 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x24 u32 u32x128x65 u32 u32x128x200 -> u32
s add p3 p1
@aw ak p2 s 0
@aw av p2 s 1
isp eq ak 2
isn eq ak 1
pi add p7 av
@rd pt p6 pi
pidx select isp pt 0
@col pio p8 17152 pidx
pio1 select isp pio 0
ng add p5 av
@rd nt p4 ng
nidx select isn nt 0
@col nio p8 17152 nidx
nio1 select isn nio 0
x or pio1 nio1
r or p0 x
ret r
end
fn shefj u32x128x24 u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32 u32x128x65 u32 u32x128x200 -> u32x128x24
g add p5 p1
@nwd op p2 g 1
@nwd na p2 g 2
@nwd af p2 g 3
@rd nty p4 g
@col tio p8 17152 nty
isrw ge op 29
iscf1 ge op 19
iscf2 le op 21
iscf and iscf1 iscf2
a fold shefa na 0 p3 af p4 p5 p6 p7 p8
ae ne a 0
ti eq tio 1
c1 or ti ae
c2 and iscf c1
e1 or isrw c2
e select e1 1 0
@wr r p0 p1 e
ret r
end
# nodeCost of op p0
fn shcost u32 -> u32
iscf1 ge p0 19
iscf2 le p0 21
iscf and iscf1 iscf2
isdv1 eq p0 10
isdv2 eq p0 11
isdv or isdv1 isdv2
ism eq p0 4
a select ism 3 1
b select isdv 8 a
r select iscf 16 b
ret r
end
# add node i to the cone state (members, counts of uses from members, cost)
fn shaddc u32x128x24 u32 u32x128x512 u32 -> u32x128x24
s add p3 p1
@aw ak p2 s 0
@aw av p2 s 1
isn eq ak 1
widx select isn av 3071
@rd old p0 widx
inc select isn 1 0
nw add old inc
@wr r p0 widx nw
ret r
end
fn shadd (u32x128x24,u32x128x24,u32) u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32 -> (u32x128x24,u32x128x24,u32)
mem at p0 0
cnt at p0 1
cost at p0 2
g add p4 p1
@nwd op p2 g 1
@nwd na p2 g 2
@nwd af p2 g 3
@wr mem2 mem p1 1
cnt2 fold shaddc na cnt p3 af
c call shcost op
cost2 add cost c
r rec mem2 cnt2 cost2
ret r
end
# the cone walk, trip t: node i = root - 1 - t joins when eligible and every use is a member.
# State as shadd; extras: nodes args nt fst retk retv uc eff sh root
fn shcw (u32x128x24,u32x128x24,u32) u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32 u32 u32 u32x128x24 u32x128x24 u32x128x200 u32 -> (u32x128x24,u32x128x24,u32)
mem at p0 0
cnt at p0 1
t1 add p1 1
i sub p11 t1
g add p5 i
@rd nty p4 g
sc lt nty 2
@rd ef p9 i
nef eq ef 0
retn1 eq p6 1
retn2 eq p7 i
retn and retn1 retn2
nret select retn false true
@col ow p10 2816 g
nown eq ow 0
@rd uc p8 i
hasu gt uc 0
@rd cn cnt i
same eq cn uc
a1 and sc nef
a2 and a1 nret
a3 and a2 nown
a4 and a3 hasu
join and a4 same
step call shadd p0 i p2 p3 p5
r select join step p0
ret r
end
# The cone of the select arm (p9 p10) against the other arm (p11 p12) and the condition
# (p13 p14): (members column, cost); empty when the arm is not an eligible private root.
fn shcone u32x128x200 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32 u32 u32 u32x128x24 u32x128x24 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> (u32x128x24,u32)
isn eq p9 1
rv select isn p10 0
gr add p4 rv
n1 eq p11 1
n1s eq p12 rv
sameo and n1 n1s
c1 eq p13 1
c1s eq p13 1
c1e eq p14 rv
samec and c1 c1e
nso select sameo false true
nsc select samec false true
@rd nty p3 gr
isc lt nty 2
@rd ef p8 rv
nef eq ef 0
retn1 eq p5 1
retn2 eq p6 rv
retn and retn1 retn2
nret select retn false true
@col ow p0 2816 gr
nown eq ow 0
@rd uc p7 rv
one eq uc 1
a1 and isn nso
a2 and a1 nsc
a3 and a2 isc
a4 and a3 nef
a5 and a4 nret
a6 and a5 nown
valid and a6 one
z call zcol
z2 call zcol
s0 rec z z2 0
sa call shadd s0 rv p1 p2 p4
st0 select valid sa s0
steps select valid rv 0
st fold shcw steps st0 p1 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 p8 p0 rv
mem at st 0
cost at st 2
r rec mem cost
ret r
end
# trip i of the member writes: node i of the function (first node p4) gets owner js + 1 and arm 1 or 2
fn shlw u32x128x200 u32 u32x128x24 u32x128x24 u32 u32 -> u32x128x200
g add p4 p1
@rd ma p2 p1
@rd mb p3 p1
ina eq ma 1
inb eq mb 1
any or ina inb
@col oo p0 2816 g
@col oa p0 5632 g
js1 add p5 1
nwo select any js1 oo
armv select ina 1 2
nwa select any armv oa
@colw s1 p0 2816 g nwo
@colw s2 s1 5632 g nwa
ret s2
end
# select nodes: the lazy arms
fn shlz u32x128x200 u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32 u32 u32 u32x128x24 u32x128x24 -> u32x128x200
g add p5 p1
@nwd op p2 g 1
@nwd af p2 g 3
@rd nty p4 g
@aw ck p3 af 0
@aw cv p3 af 1
af1 add af 1
@aw xk p3 af1 0
@aw xv p3 af1 1
af2 add af 2
@aw yk p3 af2 0
@aw yv p3 af2 1
issel eq op 18
sc lt nty 2
isl and issel sc
ra call shcone p0 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 p8 p9 xk xv yk yv ck cv
rb call shcone p0 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 p8 p9 yk yv xk xv ck cv
mema at ra 0
ca at ra 1
memb at rb 0
cb at rb 1
cgt gt ca cb
cmx select cgt ca cb
big ge cmx 8
go and isl big
n select go p1 0
r fold shlw n p0 mema memb p5 p1
ret r
end
# a missing body: chunk function p1 is added to the list of the shape table (once)
fn shmq u32 u32 u32x128x200 u32 -> u32
ki add p1 16129
@rd v p2 ki
e eq v p3
x select e 1 0
r or p0 x
ret r
end
fn shmiss u32x128x200 u32 -> u32x128x200
@rd n p0 16128
isn ne p1 4294967295
d fold shmq n 0 p0 p1
nd eq d 0
add1 and isn nd
li add n 16129
nl1 add n 1
@rd old p0 li
wv select add1 p1 old
@wr a p0 li wv
nn select add1 nl1 n
@wr b a 16128 nn
ret b
end
# node j of a function: fillRun, overwritesState, borrowLive
fn shpn u32x128x200 u32 u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x45 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x200
g add p8 p1
fr call shfill p5 p6 p4 p2 p3 p7 g
fc at fr 0
fm at fr 1
orr call shover p5 p6 p4 p2 p3 p7 g
oc at orr 0
om at orr 1
@colw s1 p0 0 g fc
@colw s2 s1 8448 g oc
@nwd op p5 g 1
@nwd af p5 g 3
@rd nty p7 g
isset eq op 26
isput eq op 28
isfold eq op 20
isloop eq op 21
sp or isset isput
fl or isfold isloop
sf or sp fl
pos select sp 0 1
slot add af pos
@aw ok p6 slot 0
@aw ov p6 slot 1
isagg ge nty 3
c1 and isagg sf
isp eq ok 2
isn eq ok 1
ds select isn ov 0
gd add p8 ds
@nwd dop p5 gd 1
d22 eq dop 22
d23 eq dop 23
d26 eq dop 26
d28 eq dop 28
da or d22 d23
db or d26 d28
dc or da db
fn1 and isn dc
fresh or isp fn1
c2 and c1 fresh
nn select c2 p11 0
self select sp 1 0
bq call shborr p5 p6 p7 nn p8 p9 ok ov p1 p10 self
@colw s3 s2 11264 g bq
s4 call shmiss s3 fm
s5 call shmiss s4 om
ret s5
end
fn shpass u32x128x200 u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x45 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32 -> u32x128x200
@fwd fst p3 p7 4
@fwd nfn p3 p7 5
@fwd rw p3 p7 6
@fwd pf p3 p7 2
retk shr rw 28
retv and rw 268435455
z call zcol
z2 call zcol
uc fold shucj nfn z p4 p5 fst
eff fold shefj nfn z2 p4 p5 p6 fst p2 pf p0
s1 fold shpn nfn p0 p1 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 fst retk retv nfn
s2 fold shlz nfn s1 p4 p5 p6 fst retk retv uc eff
ret s2
end
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fusion helpers (src/optimize.ts): funcHasIo, readByGetOnly, gets of a parameter, bodyCost,
# the state-consumer shape checks, use counts.

@zarr zbld u32x128x128 128
@zarr zmap u32x128x48 48
@zarr zcache u32x128x96 96

fn shhip u32 u32 u32x128x200 u32x128x65 u32 -> u32
pi add p4 p1
@rd t p3 pi
@col io p2 17152 t
r or p0 io
ret r
end
fn shhin u32 u32 u32x128x200 u32x128x24 u32 -> u32
g add p4 p1
@rd t p3 g
@col io p2 17152 t
r or p0 io
ret r
end
# 1 when function b = p4 has an io token in its result, parameters or node types
fn shhasio u32x128x200 u32x128x65 u32x128x45 u32x128x24 u32 -> u32
@bodyd b p2 p4
@col rio p0 17152 b_rs
a fold shhip b_np rio p0 p1 b_pf
r fold shhin b_n a p0 p3 b_f
ret r
end

# readByGetOnly: is parameter k = p4 of function b = p3 read only as the array of get nodes (and
# not returned)? 1 or 0
fn shrga u32 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32 bool -> u32
s add p3 p1
@opr a p2 s
@isop isk a_k a_v 2 p4
i0 eq p1 0
g0 and p5 i0
ng select g0 false true
bd and isk ng
b select bd 1 0
r or p0 b
ret r
end
fn shrgj u32 u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32 u32 -> u32
g add p4 p1
@nrow n p2 g
isg eq n_op 25
r fold shrga n_na p0 p3 n_af p5 isg
ret r
end
fn shrdg u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x45 u32 u32 bool -> u32
@bodyd b p2 p3
@retop r p1 b_rw
@isop rp r_k r_v 2 p4
bn select p5 b_n 0
bad fold shrgj bn 0 p0 p1 b_f p4
nb eq bad 0
nrp select rp false true
o and nb nrp
r2 select o 1 0
ret r2
end

# the gets `get p_k x` of function b = p3 whose index x is not p1: how many, and how many distinct
# operands x (by kind and value). Result (count, distinct).
fn shgd2 u32 u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32
g add p4 p1
@nrow n p2 g
isg eq n_op 25
@opk a0 p3 n_af 0
@isop is0 a0_k a0_v 2 p5
@opk a1 p3 n_af 1
@isop same a1_k a1_v p6 p7
@isop notc a1_k a1_v 2 1
nc select notc false true
c1 and isg is0
c2 and c1 nc
d and c2 same
b select d 1 0
r or p0 b
ret r
end
fn shgd1 u32 u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32 u32 -> u32
g add p4 p1
@nrow n p2 g
isg eq n_op 25
@opk a0 p3 n_af 0
@isop is0 a0_k a0_v 2 p5
@opk a1 p3 n_af 1
@isop notc a1_k a1_v 2 1
nc select notc false true
c1 and isg is0
cand and c1 nc
dup fold shgd2 p1 0 p2 p3 p4 p5 a1_k a1_v
nd eq dup 0
inc and cand nd
x select inc 1 0
r add p0 x
ret r
end
fn shgc u32 u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32 u32 -> u32
g add p4 p1
@nrow n p2 g
isg eq n_op 25
@opk a0 p3 n_af 0
@isop is0 a0_k a0_v 2 p5
@opk a1 p3 n_af 1
@isop notc a1_k a1_v 2 1
nc select notc false true
c1 and isg is0
cand and c1 nc
x select cand 1 0
r add p0 x
ret r
end
fn shgets u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x45 u32 u32 bool -> (u32,u32)
@bodyd b p2 p3
bn select p5 b_n 0
nc fold shgc bn 0 p0 p1 b_f p4
dc fold shgd1 bn 0 p0 p1 b_f p4
r rec nc dc
ret r
end

# bodyCost of function b = p2 without node p3
fn shbcs u32 u32 u32x128x128 u32 u32 -> u32
g add p3 p1
@nwd op p2 g 1
c call shcost op
isj eq p1 p4
x select isj 0 c
r add p0 x
ret r
end
fn shbcost u32x128x128 u32x128x45 u32 u32 bool -> u32
@bodyd b p1 p2
bn select p4 b_n 0
r fold shbcs bn 0 p0 b_f p3
ret r
end

# fuseIntoState: parameter 0 of function b = p3 used other than as the target of its ret set
# p5, of a guarded previous read (p4 the column) or of `get p0 p1`: (bad, some get p0 p1)
fn shfsa u32 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32x128x24 bool -> u32
s add p3 p1
@opr a p2 s
@isop isp0 a_k a_v 2 0
k0 eq p1 0
isset eq p4 p5
@rd pv p6 p4
ispv eq pv 1
o1 or isset ispv
o2 or o1 p7
good and k0 o2
bad1 select good false isp0
b select bad1 1 0
r or p0 b
ret r
end
fn shfsj (u32,u32) u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32x128x24 -> (u32,u32)
g add p4 p1
@nrow n p2 g
isg eq n_op 25
@opk a0 p3 n_af 0
@opk a1 p3 n_af 1
@isop z0 a0_k a0_v 2 0
@isop z1 a1_k a1_v 2 1
t1 and isg z0
atc and t1 z1
bad at p0 0
has at p0 1
bad2 fold shfsa n_na bad p3 n_af p1 p5 p6 atc
hx select atc 1 0
has2 or has hx
r rec bad2 has2
ret r
end
fn shfs u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x45 u32 u32x128x24 u32 bool -> (u32,u32)
@bodyd b p2 p3
s0 rec 0 0
bn select p6 b_n 0
r fold shfsj bn s0 p0 p1 b_f p5 p4
ret r
end

# the use counts of function f = p3 (nodes' operands and the ret)
fn shuses u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x45 u32 -> u32x128x24
@bodyd b p2 p3
z call zcol
u fold shucj b_n z p0 p1 b_f
@retop r p1 b_rw
isn eq r_k 1
widx select isn r_v 3071
@rd old u widx
inc select isn 1 0
nw add old inc
@wr x u widx nw
ret x
end
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BodyBuilder (src/optimize.ts). The builder BLD (u32x128x128): word 0 node count, 1 overflow
# (more than 64 nodes or 7936 operand pairs: the attempt is refused), 2 operand pair count, 3 4
# ret kind and value (set by the caller); node j at 16 + 6 j: op, operand count, callee, pred,
# type, first operand pair; operand pair s at 512 + 2 s. The copy context cx (u32x128):
#   0 first node of the copied body, 1 mode (0 copy, 1 a get of parameter kswap becomes the
#   producer's element at the mapped index, 2 it becomes the fixed operand, 3 `get p0 p1` becomes
#   the element at p1, 4 a guarded previous-element read becomes the fixed operand), 2 kswap,
#   3 the skipped node, 4 5 operand of parameter 0, 6 7 operand of parameter 1, 8 9 (kk, off2):
#   parameter i >= 2 becomes (2, i) if i < kk else (2, i + off2), 10 11 the fixed operand,
#   12 map selector (0 MAP2, 1 MAP1), 16 first node of the producer body, 17 its node count,
#   18 its ret set node, 19 its array length, 20 the first parameter of the fused body that
#   takes the producer's extras (minus 2: off2 of the producer copy).
# The copy state RS = (BLD, MAP2, MAP1, CACHE): MAP* (u32x128x48) the operand each copied node
# became (2 words a node), CACHE (u32x128x96) the element cache: count, then 4 words an entry
# (index kind, index value, element kind, element value).

# a node row (op p1, operand count p2, callee p3, pred p4, type p5) when p6; its position
fn shbadd u32x128x128 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 bool -> (u32x128x128,u32)
@rd n p0 0
@rd ov p0 1
@rd pr p0 2
full ge n 64
ovn ne ov 0
bad0 or full ovn
gn select p6 false true
bad or bad0 gn
nbad select bad false true
bm mul n 6
r0 add 16 bm
@wr w0 p0 r0 p1
r1 add r0 1
@wr w1 w0 r1 p2
r2 add r0 2
@wr w2 w1 r2 p3
r3 add r0 3
@wr w3 w2 r3 p4
r4 add r0 4
@wr w4 w3 r4 p5
r5 add r0 5
@wr w5 w4 r5 pr
n1 add n 1
nn select nbad n1 n
ovf or full ovn
ov1 select ovf 1 ov
@wr w6 w5 0 nn
@wr w7 w6 1 ov1
o rec w7 n
ret o
end
# an operand pair (p1 p2) of the node just added, when p3
fn shbpair u32x128x128 u32 u32 bool -> u32x128x128
@rd ov p0 1
@rd pr p0 2
full ge pr 7936
ovn ne ov 0
bad0 or full ovn
gn select p3 false true
bad or bad0 gn
nbad select bad false true
sl mul pr 2
i0 add 512 sl
i0s select nbad i0 8
i1 add i0 1
i1s select nbad i1 9
@wr w0 p0 i0s p1
@wr w1 w0 i1s p2
pr1 add pr 1
npr select nbad pr1 pr
ovf or full ovn
ov1 select ovf 1 ov
@wr w2 w1 2 npr
@wr w3 w2 1 ov1
ret w3
end
# the operand (p0 p1) of a copied body under the copy context p2 and map p3
fn shmapo u32 u32 u32x128 u32x128x48 -> (u32,u32)
@pg z0k p2 4
@pg z0v p2 5
@pg z1k p2 6
@pg z1v p2 7
@pg kk p2 8
@pg off2 p2 9
isp eq p0 2
isn eq p0 1
i0 eq p1 0
i1 eq p1 1
lt lt p1 kk
v2 add p1 off2
pv select lt p1 v2
pk1 select i1 z1k 2
pk select i0 z0k pk1
pv1 select i1 z1v pv
pvv select i0 z0v pv1
mi mul p1 2
@rd mk p3 mi
mi1 add mi 1
@rd mv p3 mi1
nk0 select isn mk p0
nv0 select isn mv p1
nk select isp pk nk0
nv select isp pvv nv0
r rec nk nv
ret r
end
# operand step k of a copied node: map it and add it (p0 BLD; args, first operand, cx, map)
fn shcpa u32x128x128 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32x128 u32x128x48 bool -> u32x128x128
@opk a p2 p3 p1
m call shmapo a_k a_v p4 p5
mk at m 0
mv at m 1
r call shbpair p0 mk mv p6
ret r
end
# the element cache: entry p1 matches the index (p3 p4)? State: the match + 1 or 0
fn shelc u32 u32 u32x128x96 u32 u32 -> u32
e mul p1 4
i0 add 4 e
@rd k p2 i0
i1 add i0 1
@rd v p2 i1
@isop m k v p3 p4
z eq p0 0
t and m z
n1 add p1 1
r select t n1 p0
ret r
end

#@template shcopy
fn %NAME% (u32x128x128,u32x128x48,u32x128x48,u32x128x96) u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32x128 u32x128x24 -> (u32x128x128,u32x128x48,u32x128x48,u32x128x96)
@pg bf p5 0
@pg mode p5 1
@pg kswap p5 2
@pg skipj p5 3
@pg mapsel p5 12
@pg fk p5 10
@pg fv p5 11
g add bf p1
@nrow n p2 g
@rd nty p4 g
@opk a0 p3 n_af 0
@opk a1 p3 n_af 1
isget eq n_op 25
@isop a0k a0_k a0_v 2 kswap
@isop a0z a0_k a0_v 2 0
@isop a1o a1_k a1_v 2 1
gk and isget a0k
gz and isget a0z
atc and gz a1o
isskip eq p1 skipj
@rd pv p6 p1
ispv eq pv 1
m1 eq mode 1
m2 eq mode 2
m3 eq mode 3
m4 eq mode 4
f2 and m2 gk
f4 and m4 ispv
fixed or f2 f4
e1 and m1 gk
e3 and m3 atc
elem or e1 e3
use0 eq mapsel 0
mp2 at p0 1
mp1 at p0 2
mcur select use0 mp2 mp1
?ix call shmapo a1_k a1_v p5 mcur
?ixk at ix 0
?ixv at ix 1
?ek select e3 2 ixk
?ev select e3 1 ixv
?el call shelem p0 ek ev elem p2 p3 p4 p5
?bld1 at el 0
?mp21 at el 1
?mp11 at el 2
?cache1 at el 3
?erk at el 4
?erv at el 5
!bld1 at p0 0
!mp21 mov mp2
!mp11 mov mp1
!cache1 at p0 3
!erk mov 0
!erv mov 0
mcur1 select use0 mp21 mp11
sk1 select isskip true fixed
sk2 select sk1 true elem
doadd select sk2 false true
ad call shbadd bld1 n_op n_na n_ce n_pd nty doadd
bld2 at ad 0
pos at ad 1
na1 select doadd n_na 0
bld3 fold shcpa na1 bld2 p3 n_af p5 mcur1 doadd
nk select fixed fk 1
nk2 select elem erk nk
nv select fixed fv pos
nv2 select elem erv nv
nk3 select isskip 0 nk2
nv3 select isskip 0 nv2
mi mul p1 2
mi1 add mi 1
@wr mw0 mcur1 mi nk3
@wr mw1 mw0 mi1 nv3
mp2n select use0 mw1 mp21
mp1n select use0 mp11 mw1
r rec bld3 mp2n mp1n cache1
ret r
end
#@end
@inst shcopy shcp1 NEST=0
# the producer's element at the operand (p1 p2) when p3 (the elementBuilder of src/optimize.ts):
# the cached one, else the reduction of the index to the array length and a copy of the producer
# body (p4 nodes, p5 args, p6 ntys, p7 cx). Result (RS, element kind, element value).
fn shelem (u32x128x128,u32x128x48,u32x128x48,u32x128x96) u32 u32 bool u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32x128 -> (u32x128x128,u32x128x48,u32x128x48,u32x128x96,u32,u32)
bld at p0 0
mp2 at p0 1
mp1 at p0 2
cache at p0 3
@rd cnt cache 0
fnd fold shelc cnt 0 cache p1 p2
found ne fnd 0
nf select found false true
need and p3 nf
@isop isp1 p1 p2 2 1
@pg len p7 19
l1 eq len 1
lm1 sub len 1
lan and len lm1
pow2 eq lan 0
nisp select isp1 false true
needred and need nisp
nl1 select l1 false true
needn and needred nl1
opc select pow2 5 11
lit select pow2 lm1 len
ad call shbadd bld opc 2 0 0 0 needn
b1 at ad 0
pos at ad 1
b2 call shbpair b1 p1 p2 needn
b3 call shbpair b2 3 lit needn
ik0 select l1 3 1
ik select isp1 2 ik0
iv0 select l1 0 pos
iv select isp1 1 iv0
@pg b1f p7 16
@pg b1n p7 17
@pg b1s p7 18
@pg base p7 20
z call zpage
c0 set z 0 b1f
c3 set c0 3 b1s
c6 set c3 6 ik
c7 set c6 7 iv
off1 sub base 2
c9 set c7 9 off1
c12 set c9 12 1
trips select need b1n 0
st0 rec b3 mp2 mp1 cache
zc call zcol
st1 fold shcp1 trips st0 p4 p5 p6 c12 zc
bld4 at st1 0
mp24 at st1 1
mp14 at st1 2
cache4 at st1 3
g add b1f b1s
@nwd saf p4 g 3
s2 add saf 2
@opr sv p5 s2
mv call shmapo sv_k sv_v c12 mp14
mvk at mv 0
mvv at mv 1
ei mul cnt 4
e0 add 4 ei
e1 add e0 1
e2 add e0 2
e3 add e0 3
e0s select need e0 1
e1s select need e1 1
e2s select need e2 1
e3s select need e3 1
@wr q0 cache4 e0s p1
@wr q1 q0 e1s p2
@wr q2 q1 e2s mvk
@wr q3 q2 e3s mvv
cnt1 add cnt 1
ncnt select need cnt1 cnt
@wr q4 q3 0 ncnt
fi sub fnd 1
fe mul fi 4
fb add 4 fe
fr2 add fb 2
fr3 add fb 3
@rd ck cache fr2
@rd cv cache fr3
rk select found ck mvk
rv select found cv mvv
r rec bld4 mp24 mp14 q4 rk rv
ret r
end
@inst shcopy shcps NEST=1
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The three fusions (fuseExtra, fuseIntoState, fuseRecurrence) as attempts at a site. The site
# page st (u32x128): 0 first node of the function, 1 producer body, 2 consumer body, 3 k,
# 4 producer node, 5 consumer node, 6 n1, 7 n2, 8 array length, 11 consumer operand count,
# 12 its first operand, 13 the producer's first operand, 14 the producer's operand count,
# 15 recordState, 16 the consumer's type. An attempt gives (BLD, INF): INF (u32x128x2) word 0 ok,
# 1 kind (1 extra, 2 state, 3 recurrence), 2 parameter count of the fused body, 3 its result
# type, 4 operand count of the replacement fold, 5 consumer node, 6 producer node, 7 k, 8 the
# consumer's type, 9 1 when the type of the (state, previous) record is to be interned (the
# placeholder 4294967280 is used for it), 10 the state type; 16.. its parameter types; 128..
# the replacement fold's operand pairs (kind 9: a replacement node of the recurrence, value its
# index).

@zarr zinf u32x128x2 2

# parameter types of the fused body: body2's (except k, and parameter 0 when p5), then
fn shpa u32x128x2 u32 u32x128x65 u32 u32 bool -> u32x128x2
pi add p3 p1
@rd t p2 pi
isk eq p1 p4
lt lt p1 p4
im1 sub p1 1
pos select lt p1 im1
i0 eq p1 0
sk0 and p5 i0
skip or isk sk0
idx0 add 16 pos
idx select skip 15 idx0
@wr r p0 idx t
ret r
end
fn shpb u32x128x2 u32 u32x128x65 u32 u32 -> u32x128x2
a add p3 2
pi add a p1
@rd t p2 pi
bi add p4 p1
idx add 16 bi
@wr r p0 idx t
ret r
end
fn shpc u32x128x2 u32 u32x128x65 u32 -> u32x128x2
pi add p3 p1
@rd t p2 pi
idx add 16 p1
@wr r p0 idx t
ret r
end
# consumer operand i (of p4 = k removed): lo = p6, position base0 = p5 + i - lo - (i > k)
fn shpf u32x128x2 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x2
s add p3 p1
@opr a p2 s
ge ge p1 p6
isk eq p1 p4
nk select isk false true
el and ge nk
gk gt p1 p4
d select gk 1 0
b1 sub p1 p6
b2 add p5 b1
pos sub b2 d
i0 mul pos 2
ix add 128 i0
ix1 add ix 1
ixa select el ix 14
ixb select el ix1 15
@wr w0 p0 ixa a_k
@wr w1 w0 ixb a_v
ret w1
end
# producer extra i: operand 2 + i of the producer, at position p4 + i
fn shpg u32x128x2 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32 -> u32x128x2
a add p3 2
s add a p1
@opr x p2 s
q add p4 p1
q2 mul q 2
ix add 128 q2
ix1 add ix 1
@wr w0 p0 ix x_k
@wr w1 w0 ix1 x_v
ret w1
end
# does consumer extra operand i equal operand 1 (p4 p5)?
fn shsq u32 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 -> u32
a add p3 2
s add a p1
@opr x p2 s
@isop m x_k x_v p4 p5
b select m 1 0
r or p0 b
ret r
end

# fuseExtra: p0 nodes p1 args p2 fns p3 tl p4 nt p5 st p6 go
fn shatx u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x45 u32x128x65 u32x128x24 u32x128 bool -> (u32x128x128,u32x128x2)
@pg ff p5 0
@pg b1 p5 1
@pg b2 p5 2
@pg k p5 3
@pg pi p5 4
@pg ci p5 5
@pg n1 p5 6
@pg n2 p5 7
@pg len p5 8
@pg nc p5 11
@pg caf p5 12
@pg paf p5 13
@pg np p5 14
@pg cty p5 16
@bodyd d1 p2 b1
@bodyd d2 p2 b2
sp call shprod p0 p1 p2 b1 p6
st1 at sp 1
setj1 at sp 4
pure eq st1 2
rdg call shrdg p0 p1 p2 b2 k p6
rdgb eq rdg 1
gt call shgets p0 p1 p2 b2 k p6
nct at gt 0
dct at gt 1
atc eq nct 0
lel le n2 n1
eql eq n1 len
c1 select atc lel eql
cost call shbcost p0 p2 b1 setj1 p6
prod mul dct cost
c2 le prod 4
kge ge k 2
a0 and pure c1
a1 and a0 c2
a2 and a1 rdgb
a3 and a2 kge
ok0 and a3 p6
z call zbld
zm call zmap
zm2 call zmap
zca call zcache
rs0 rec z zm zm2 zca
zp call zpage
x0 set zp 0 d2_f
x1 set x0 1 1
x2 set x1 2 k
x3 set x2 3 4294967295
x4 set x3 4 2
x6 set x4 6 2
x7 set x6 7 1
x8 set x7 8 k
x9 set x8 9 4294967295
x16 set x9 16 d1_f
x17 set x16 17 d1_n
x18 set x17 18 setj1
x19 set x18 19 len
npm1 sub d2_np 1
cx set x19 20 npm1
trips select ok0 d2_n 0
zc call zcol
rs1 fold shcps trips rs0 p0 p1 p4 cx zc
bld1 at rs1 0
mp2 at rs1 1
@retop rr p1 d2_rw
rm call shmapo rr_k rr_v cx mp2
rk at rm 0
rv at rm 1
@wr b3 bld1 3 rk
@wr b4 b3 4 rv
@rd bn b4 0
@rd bo b4 1
nsm le bn 48
nov eq bo 0
szok and nsm nov
ok and ok0 szok
oki select ok 1 0
inf0 call zinf
@wr i0 inf0 0 oki
@wr i1 i0 1 1
np1b sub d1_np 2
np1g select p6 np1b 0
npr add npm1 np1b
@wr i2 i1 2 npr
@wr i3 i2 3 d2_rs
nm1 sub nc 1
npp sub np 2
nppg select p6 npp 0
nra add nm1 npp
@wr i4 i3 4 nra
@wr i5 i4 5 ci
@wr i6 i5 6 pi
@wr i7 i6 7 k
@wr i8 i7 8 cty
pa fold shpa d2_np i8 p3 d2_pf k false
pb fold shpb np1g pa p3 d1_pf npm1
pf fold shpf nc pb p1 caf k 0 0
pg fold shpg nppg pf p1 paf nm1
r rec b4 pg
ret r
end

# fuseIntoState (k == 1)
fn shats u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x45 u32x128x65 u32x128x24 u32x128 bool -> (u32x128x128,u32x128x2)
@pg ff p5 0
@pg b1 p5 1
@pg b2 p5 2
@pg k p5 3
@pg pi p5 4
@pg ci p5 5
@pg n1 p5 6
@pg n2 p5 7
@pg len p5 8
@pg nc p5 11
@pg caf p5 12
@pg paf p5 13
@pg np p5 14
@pg cty p5 16
@bodyd d1 p2 b1
@bodyd d2 p2 b2
sp call shprod p0 p1 p2 b1 p6
st1 at sp 1
setj1 at sp 4
pure eq st1 2
sp2 call shprod p0 p1 p2 b2 p6
prev2 at sp2 0
gdef2 at sp2 2
sok2 at sp2 3
setj2 at sp2 4
fsr call shfs p0 p1 p2 b2 prev2 setj2 p6
fbad at fsr 0
fhas at fsr 1
caf1 add caf 1
@opr c1 p1 caf1
nex sub nc 2
nexg select p6 nex 0
dq fold shsq nexg 0 p1 caf c1_k c1_v
noeq eq dq 0
isk1 eq k 1
n1l eq n1 len
n2l eq n2 len
gd eq gdef2 1
so eq sok2 1
fb0 eq fbad 0
fh eq fhas 1
a0 and pure isk1
a1 and a0 n1l
a2 and a1 n2l
a3 and a2 noeq
a4 and a3 gd
a5 and a4 so
a6 and a5 fb0
a7 and a6 fh
ok0 and a7 p6
z call zbld
zm call zmap
zm2 call zmap
zca call zcache
rs0 rec z zm zm2 zca
zp call zpage
x0 set zp 0 d2_f
x1 set x0 1 3
x2 set x1 3 4294967295
x4 set x2 4 2
x6 set x4 6 2
x7 set x6 7 1
x16 set x7 16 d1_f
x17 set x16 17 d1_n
x18 set x17 18 setj1
x19 set x18 19 len
cx set x19 20 d2_np
trips select ok0 d2_n 0
zc call zcol
rs1 fold shcps trips rs0 p0 p1 p4 cx zc
bld1 at rs1 0
mp2 at rs1 1
@retop rr p1 d2_rw
rm call shmapo rr_k rr_v cx mp2
rk at rm 0
rv at rm 1
@wr b3 bld1 3 rk
@wr b4 b3 4 rv
@rd bn b4 0
@rd bo b4 1
nsm le bn 48
nov eq bo 0
szok and nsm nov
ok and ok0 szok
oki select ok 1 0
inf0 call zinf
@wr i0 inf0 0 oki
@wr i1 i0 1 2
np1b sub d1_np 2
np1g select p6 np1b 0
npr add d2_np np1b
@wr i2 i1 2 npr
@wr i3 i2 3 d2_rs
npp sub np 2
nppg select p6 npp 0
nra add nc npp
@wr i4 i3 4 nra
@wr i5 i4 5 ci
@wr i6 i5 6 pi
@wr i7 i6 7 k
@wr i8 i7 8 cty
pa fold shpc d2_np i8 p3 d2_pf
pb fold shpb np1g pa p3 d1_pf d2_np
@opr q0 p1 caf
paf1 add paf 1
@opr q1 p1 paf1
@wr h0 pb 128 q0_k
@wr h1 h0 129 q0_v
@wr h2 h1 130 q1_k
@wr h3 h2 131 q1_v
pf fold shpf nc h3 p1 caf 4294967295 2 2
pg fold shpg nppg pf p1 paf nc
r rec b4 pg
ret r
end

# fuseRecurrence (k >= 2, recordState): the record type is interned by the caller
fn shatr u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x45 u32x128x65 u32x128x24 u32x128 bool -> (u32x128x128,u32x128x2)
@pg ff p5 0
@pg b1 p5 1
@pg b2 p5 2
@pg k p5 3
@pg pi p5 4
@pg ci p5 5
@pg n1 p5 6
@pg n2 p5 7
@pg len p5 8
@pg nc p5 11
@pg caf p5 12
@pg paf p5 13
@pg np p5 14
@pg rsf p5 15
@pg cty p5 16
@bodyd d1 p2 b1
@bodyd d2 p2 b2
sp call shprod p0 p1 p2 b1 p6
prev1 at sp 0
st1 at sp 1
setj1 at sp 4
imp eq st1 1
rdg call shrdg p0 p1 p2 b2 k p6
rdgb eq rdg 1
gt call shgets p0 p1 p2 b2 k p6
nct at gt 0
atc eq nct 0
@rd s2 p3 d2_pf
s2sc lt s2 2
n21 le n2 n1
kge ge k 2
rsb eq rsf 1
a0 and imp rdgb
a1 and a0 atc
a2 and a1 s2sc
a3 and a2 n21
a4 and a3 kge
a5 and a4 rsb
ok0 and a5 p6
z call zbld
bs1 call shbadd z 27 2 0 0 s2 true
bs1b at bs1 0
bs2 call shbpair bs1b 2 0 true
bs3 call shbpair bs2 3 0 true
bs4 call shbadd bs3 27 2 0 0 0 true
bs4b at bs4 0
bs5 call shbpair bs4b 2 0 true
bs6 call shbpair bs5 3 1 true
zm call zmap
zm2 call zmap
zca call zcache
rs0 rec bs6 zm zm2 zca
zp call zpage
y0 set zp 0 d1_f
y1 set y0 1 4
y3 set y1 3 setj1
y4 set y3 4 2
y6 set y4 6 2
y7 set y6 7 1
y10 set y7 10 1
y11 set y10 11 1
y12 set y11 12 1
np3 sub d2_np 3
cx1 set y12 9 np3
t1 select ok0 d1_n 0
rs1 fold shcp1 t1 rs0 p0 p1 p4 cx1 prev1
mp1 at rs1 2
gsn add d1_f setj1
@nwd ssf p0 gsn 3
s2x add ssf 2
@opr sv p1 s2x
em call shmapo sv_k sv_v cx1 mp1
ek at em 0
ev at em 1
w0 set zp 0 d2_f
w1 set w0 1 2
w2 set w1 2 k
w3 set w2 3 4294967295
w4 set w3 4 1
w5 set w4 5 0
w6 set w5 6 2
w7 set w6 7 1
w8 set w7 8 k
w9 set w8 9 4294967295
w10 set w9 10 ek
w11 set w10 11 ev
t2 select ok0 d2_n 0
zc call zcol
rs2 fold shcp1 t2 rs1 p0 p1 p4 w11 zc
bld2 at rs2 0
mp2 at rs2 1
@retop rr p1 d2_rw
rm call shmapo rr_k rr_v w11 mp2
rk at rm 0
rv at rm 1
pr1 call shbadd bld2 23 2 0 0 4294967280 true
pr1b at pr1 0
prpos at pr1 1
pr2 call shbpair pr1b rk rv true
pr3 call shbpair pr2 ek ev true
@wr b3 pr3 3 1
@wr b4 b3 4 prpos
@rd bn b4 0
@rd bo b4 1
nsm le bn 48
nov eq bo 0
szok and nsm nov
ok and ok0 szok
oki select ok 1 0
inf0 call zinf
@wr i0 inf0 0 oki
@wr i1 i0 1 3
np1b sub d1_np 2
np1g select p6 np1b 0
npm1 sub d2_np 1
npr add npm1 np1b
@wr i2 i1 2 npr
@wr i3 i2 3 4294967280
npp sub np 2
nppg select p6 npp 0
nra0 add nc npp
nra sub nra0 1
@wr i4 i3 4 nra
@wr i5 i4 5 ci
@wr i6 i5 6 pi
@wr i7 i6 7 k
@wr i8 i7 8 cty
@wr i9 i8 9 1
@wr i10 i9 10 s2
@wr i16 i10 16 4294967280
pa fold shpa d2_np i16 p3 d2_pf k true
pb fold shpb np1g pa p3 d1_pf npm1
@opr q0 p1 caf
@wr h0 pb 128 q0_k
@wr h1 h0 129 q0_v
@wr h2 h1 130 9
@wr h3 h2 131 0
pf fold shpf nc h3 p1 caf k 2 2
nm1 sub nc 1
pg fold shpg nppg pf p1 paf nm1
r rec b4 pg
ret r
end
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# fuseOnce: the first site (consumer node in order, then its operand k) at which an attempt
# succeeds. SR = (found, BLD, INF, missing): the first body that was needed and is absent.

# operand k of consumer ci (p10), first node p11, recordState p12; uses p9
fn shfk (u32,u32x128x128,u32x128x2,u32) u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x45 u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x24 u32x128x200 u32x128x24 u32 u32 u32 -> (u32,u32x128x128,u32x128x2,u32)
found at p0 0
bld at p0 1
inf at p0 2
miss at p0 3
nf eq found 0
gc add p11 p10
@nrow c p2 gc
@rd cty p7 gc
@opk n2a p3 c_af 0
isfold eq c_op 20
n2l eq n2a_k 3
@fwd rw2 p4 c_ce 6
has2 ne rw2 0
@opk a p3 c_af p1
isn eq a_k 1
@col u p9 0 a_v
one eq u 1
pi select isn a_v 0
gp add p11 pi
@nrow pr p2 gp
@rd pty p7 gp
isf eq pr_op 20
kpos gt p1 0
@opk n1a p3 pr_af 0
n1l eq n1a_k 3
@ty ptag p5 pty 0
@ty plen p5 pty 1
@ty pel p5 pty 2
isarr eq ptag 4
eu eq pel 0
@fwd rw1 p4 pr_ce 6
has1 ne rw1 0
n1le le n1a_v plen
hio2 call shhasio p8 p6 p4 p7 c_ce
hio1 call shhasio p8 p6 p4 p7 pr_ce
nio2 eq hio2 0
nio1 eq hio1 0
c0 and nf isfold
c1 and c0 n2l
c2 and c1 kpos
c3 and c2 isn
c4 and c3 one
cand0 and c4 isf
sp call shprod p2 p3 p4 pr_ce cand0
st1 at sp 1
sok ne st1 0
nh2 select has2 false true
miss2 and cand0 nh2
p1a and n1l isarr
p1b and p1a eu
p1c and p1b n1le
nh1 select has1 false true
m1a and cand0 has2
m1b and m1a p1c
miss1 and m1b nh1
mid0 select miss1 pr_ce 4294967295
mid select miss2 c_ce mid0
nomiss eq miss 4294967295
nm0 ne mid 4294967295
newm and nomiss nm0
miss2v select newm mid miss
d1 and cand0 has2
d2 and d1 nio2
d3 and d2 p1c
d4 and d3 has1
d5 and d4 nio1
cond and d5 sok
zp call zpage
t0 set zp 0 p11
t1 set t0 1 pr_ce
t2 set t1 2 c_ce
t3 set t2 3 p1
t4 set t3 4 pi
t5 set t4 5 p10
t6 set t5 6 n1a_v
t7 set t6 7 n2a_v
t8 set t7 8 plen
t11 set t8 11 c_na
t12 set t11 12 c_af
t13 set t12 13 pr_af
t14 set t13 14 pr_na
t15 set t14 15 p12
st set t15 16 cty
rx call shatx p2 p3 p4 p6 p7 st cond
rs call shats p2 p3 p4 p6 p7 st cond
rr call shatr p2 p3 p4 p6 p7 st cond
bx at rx 0
ix at rx 1
bs at rs 0
is at rs 1
br at rr 0
ir at rr 1
@rd okx ix 0
@rd oks is 0
@rd okr ir 0
ux eq okx 1
nux select ux false true
us0 eq oks 1
us and nux us0
nus select us false true
ur0 eq okr 1
ur1 and nux nus
ur and ur1 ur0
any0 or ux us
any or any0 ur
bsel0 select ur br bld
bsel1 select us bs bsel0
bsel select ux bx bsel1
isel0 select ur ir inf
isel1 select us is isel0
isel select ux ix isel1
nfb eq found 0
take and nfb any
nbld select take bsel bld
ninf select take isel inf
fnn select take 1 found
r rec fnn nbld ninf miss2v
ret r
end
# consumer node ci
fn shfc (u32,u32x128x128,u32x128x2,u32) u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x45 u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x24 u32x128x200 u32x128x24 u32 u32 -> (u32,u32x128x128,u32x128x2,u32)
found at p0 0
gc add p10 p1
@nrow c p2 gc
isfold eq c_op 20
nf eq found 0
go and isfold nf
n select go c_na 0
r fold shfk n p0 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 p8 p9 p1 p10 p11
ret r
end
fn shfsearch u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x45 u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x24 u32x128x200 u32 u32 -> (u32,u32x128x128,u32x128x2,u32)
@bodyd d p2 p7
uses call shuses p0 p1 p2 p7
hio call shhasio p6 p4 p2 p5 p7
nh eq hio 0
n select nh d_n 0
z call zbld
zi call zinf
sr0 rec 0 z zi 4294967295
r fold shfc n sr0 p0 p1 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 uses d_f p8
ret r
end
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The record type of fuseRecurrence (state p4, u32): found in the types table or appended.
# (ty tl nty ntl s2 go) -> (ty, tl, type index, nty, ntl)

fn shtyf u32 u32 u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32 -> u32
@ty tag p2 p1 0
@ty ta p2 p1 1
@ty tb p2 p1 2
isr eq tag 5
two eq tb 2
@rd f0 p3 ta
ta1 add ta 1
@rd f1 p3 ta1
e0 eq f0 p4
e1 eq f1 0
m1 and isr two
m2 and m1 e0
m and m2 e1
z eq p0 0
t and m z
i1 add p1 1
r select t i1 p0
ret r
end
fn shtyrec u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32 u32 u32 bool -> (u32x384x65,u32x128x65,u32,u32,u32)
fnd fold shtyf p2 0 p0 p1 p4
found ne fnd 0
nf select found false true
app and p5 nf
@tyw a p0 p2 0 5
@tyw b a p2 1 p3
@tyw c b p2 2 2
@wr l0 p1 p3 p4
t1 add p3 1
@wr l1 l0 t1 0
fm1 sub fnd 1
idx select found fm1 p2
n1 add p2 1
n2 add p3 2
nty select app n1 p2
ntl select app n2 p3
r rec c l1 idx nty ntl
ret r
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Function images (the format of the optimizer's single-function result): u32x128x512, word 0
# code, 1 node count n, 2 3 ret kind and value, 4 literalIterations, 5 operand pair count; node j
# at 8 + 5 j: op, operand count, callee, pred, type; operand pair s at 8 + 5 n + 2 s. Node
# operand values are positions. The builder BLD as an image:

fn shbr u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x128 -> u32x128x512
b mul p1 6
s add 16 b
d mul p1 5
t add 8 d
@rd v0 p2 s
s1 add s 1
@rd v1 p2 s1
s2 add s 2
@rd v2 p2 s2
s3 add s 3
@rd v3 p2 s3
s4 add s 4
@rd v4 p2 s4
@wr w0 p0 t v0
t1 add t 1
@wr w1 w0 t1 v1
t2 add t 2
@wr w2 w1 t2 v2
t3 add t 3
@wr w3 w2 t3 v3
t4 add t 4
@wr w4 w3 t4 v4
ret w4
end
fn shbp u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x128 u32 -> u32x128x512
a mul p1 2
s add 512 a
@rd k p2 s
s1 add s 1
@rd v p2 s1
d mul p3 5
base add 8 d
o add base a
@wr w0 p0 o k
o1 add o 1
@wr w1 w0 o1 v
ret w1
end
fn shb2im u32x128x128 -> u32x128x512
@rd n p0 0
@rd pairs p0 2
@rd rk p0 3
@rd rv p0 4
z call z512
@wr h1 z 1 n
@wr h2 h1 2 rk
@wr h3 h2 3 rv
@wr h5 h3 5 pairs
a fold shbr n h5 p0
r fold shbp pairs a p0 n
ret r
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Installers: the image p1 as the body of a function, written at node row nd, operand slot ad.
# All of them do nothing when go is false.

# nodes: rows nd + j (state: nodes, running operand slot)
fn shinn1 (u32x128x128,u32) u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32 -> (u32x128x128,u32)
nodes at p0 0
run at p0 1
@rd n p2 1
d mul p1 5
t add 8 d
@rd op p2 t
t1 add t 1
@rd na p2 t1
t2 add t 2
@rd ce p2 t2
t3 add t 3
@rd pd p2 t3
g add p3 p1
gm mul g 6
i0 add gm 1
@wr w1 nodes i0 op
i1 add gm 2
@wr w2 w1 i1 na
i2 add gm 3
sl add run p4
@wr w3 w2 i2 sl
i3 add gm 4
@wr w4 w3 i3 ce
i4 add gm 5
@wr w5 w4 i4 pd
i5 add gm 0
@wr w6 w5 i5 0
nrun add run na
r rec w6 nrun
ret r
end
fn shinn u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32 u32 bool -> u32x128x128
@rd n p1 1
c select p4 n 0
s0 rec p0 0
r fold shinn1 c s0 p1 p2 p3
x at r 0
ret x
end
# operand pairs at ad + s; a ret literal of 2^28 or more takes the slot after them
fn shina1 u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x512 u32 -> u32x128x512
@rd n p2 1
d mul n 5
base add 8 d
a mul p1 2
o add base a
@rd k p2 o
o1 add o 1
@rd v p2 o1
sl add p3 p1
sa mul sl 2
sb add sa 1
@wr w0 p0 sa k
@wr w1 w0 sb v
ret w1
end
fn shina u32x128x512 u32x128x512 u32 bool -> u32x128x512
@rd pairs p1 5
@rd rk p1 2
@rd rv p1 3
c select p3 pairs 0
a fold shina1 c p0 p1 p2
big ge rv 268435456
lit and big p3
sl add p2 pairs
sa mul sl 2
sb add sa 1
@wrs w0 a sa rk lit
@wrs w1 w0 sb rv lit
ret w1
end
fn shint1 u32x128x24 u32 u32x128x512 u32 -> u32x128x24
d mul p1 5
t add 8 d
t4 add t 4
@rd ty p2 t4
g add p3 p1
@wr r p0 g ty
ret r
end
fn shint u32x128x24 u32x128x512 u32 bool -> u32x128x24
@rd n p1 1
c select p3 n 0
r fold shint1 c p0 p1 p2
ret r
end
# the row of function p1 set up from the image p2 (parameters p4 at tlist p3, result p5, first
# node p6, first operand p7): all seven words
fn shinf u32x128x45 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 bool -> u32x128x45
@rd n p2 1
@rd pairs p2 5
@rd rk p2 2
@rd rv p2 3
big ge rv 268435456
sl add p7 pairs
k5 mul 5 268435456
v5 add k5 sl
kk mul rk 268435456
v0 add kk rv
ret6 select big v5 v0
f7 mul p1 7
@wrs w0 p0 f7 1 p8
a1 add f7 1
@wrs w1 w0 a1 p4 p8
a2 add f7 2
@wrs w2 w1 a2 p3 p8
a3 add f7 3
@wrs w3 w2 a3 p5 p8
a4 add f7 4
@wrs w4 w3 a4 p6 p8
a5 add f7 5
@wrs w5 w4 a5 n p8
a6 add f7 6
@wrs w6 w5 a6 ret6 p8
ret w6
end
# only the node range and ret of function p1 (words 4 5 6) from the image p2 (first node p3, first operand p4)
fn shinf2 u32x128x45 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32 bool -> u32x128x45
@rd n p2 1
@rd pairs p2 5
@rd rk p2 2
@rd rv p2 3
big ge rv 268435456
sl add p4 pairs
k5 mul 5 268435456
v5 add k5 sl
kk mul rk 268435456
v0 add kk rv
ret6 select big v5 v0
f7 mul p1 7
a4 add f7 4
@wrs w4 p0 a4 p3 p5
a5 add f7 5
@wrs w5 w4 a5 n p5
a6 add f7 6
@wrs w6 w5 a6 ret6 p5
ret w6
end
# the node range and ret of function p1 and its word 0 (1 + 2 literalIterations of the image)
fn shinf3 u32x128x45 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32 bool -> u32x128x45
@rd li p2 4
l2 mul li 2
l3 add l2 1
f7 mul p1 7
@wrs w0 p0 f7 l3 p5
r call shinf2 w0 p1 p2 p3 p4 p5
ret r
end
# parameter types of the new function (INF word 16 + i) at tlist p2 + i
fn shinl1 u32x128x65 u32 u32x128x2 u32 -> u32x128x65
i add 16 p1
@rd t p2 i
d add p3 p1
@wr r p0 d t
ret r
end
fn shinl u32x128x65 u32x128x2 u32 bool -> u32x128x65
@rd np p1 2
c select p3 np 0
r fold shinl1 c p0 p1 p2
ret r
end
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# rewriteTop: function f without the producer (node pi), the consumer (node ci) replaced by the
# fused fold (kind 1 2) or by the three nodes rec, fold, at (kind 3), and without what only
# the producer used, as an image. Positions are of the combined list: old nodes in order
# without pi, and the replacement nodes at ci - 1 + r; the old consumer stands for the last
# replacement. INF (see shatx): word 11 the function index of the fused body.

# combined index of old node q (consumer ci, producer pi, R replacement nodes)
fn shoc u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32
lt lt p0 p1
gt gt p0 p2
d select gt 1 0
a sub p0 d
b2 add p0 p3
b sub b2 2
r select lt a b
ret r
end
# operand j of replacement node r (kind p2; consumer first operand p5): (kind, value), kind 9 a
# replacement node
fn shrwo u32x128x2 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> (u32,u32)
a mul p4 2
ix add 128 a
ix1 add ix 1
@rd rak p0 ix
@rd rav p0 ix1
is3 eq p2 3
r0 eq p3 0
r1 eq p3 1
j0 eq p4 0
c1s add p5 1
@opr c1 p1 c1s
q0k select j0 c1_k 3
q0v select j0 c1_v 0
q2k select j0 9 3
q2v select j0 1 0
k02 select r0 q0k q2k
v02 select r0 q0v q2v
kk3 select r1 rak k02
vv3 select r1 rav v02
k select is3 kk3 rak
v select is3 vv3 rav
r rec k v
ret r
end
fn shrwm1 u32x128x24 u32 u32x128x512 u32x128x2 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x24
o call shrwo p3 p2 p4 p5 p1 p6
ok at o 0
ov at o 1
isn eq ok 1
isr eq ok 9
oc call shoc ov p7 p8 p9
ca sub p7 1
rc add ca ov
idx0 select isn oc rc
act or isn isr
idx select act idx0 3071
@wrs r p0 idx 1 act
ret r
end
fn shrwm2 u32x128x24 u32 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x24
s add p3 p1
@opr a p2 s
isn eq a_k 1
oc call shoc a_v p4 p5 p6
idx select isn oc 3071
@wrs r p0 idx 1 isn
ret r
end
# liveness, trip t = M - 1 - c: p2 nodes p3 args p4 inf p5 first node p6 M p7 ci p8 pi p9 R
# p10 kind p11 consumer first operand p12 replacement operand count
fn shrwl u32x128x24 u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x2 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x24
tt add p1 1
c sub p6 tt
ca sub p7 1
@rd live p0 c
lv eq live 1
ge ge c ca
cr add ca p9
lt2 lt c cr
isrepl and ge lt2
cltca lt c ca
cpi ge c p8
dpi select cpi 1 0
jlo add c dpi
jhi0 sub c p9
jhi add jhi0 2
jold select cltca jlo jhi
nrepl select isrepl false true
g add p5 jold
@nrow n p2 g
doold and lv nrepl
no select doold n_na 0
lv2 fold shrwm2 no p0 p3 n_af p7 p8 p9
r sub c ca
is3 eq p10 3
r1 eq r 1
nr3 select r1 p12 2
nrk select is3 nr3 p12
dorep and lv isrepl
nn select dorep nrk 0
lv3 fold shrwm1 nn lv2 p3 p4 p10 r p11 p7 p8 p9
ret lv3
end
# new positions: state (RK, count)
fn shrwr (u32x128x24,u32) u32 u32x128x24 -> (u32x128x24,u32)
rk at p0 0
run at p0 1
@wr w rk p1 run
@rd l p2 p1
n add run l
r rec w n
ret r
end
# operand i of the node of combined index c as its image operand (p0 image state)
# p2 args p3 inf p4 isrepl p5 kind p6 r p7 consumer first operand p8 node first operand
# p9 ci p10 pi p11 R p12 RK p13 n'
fn shrwe1 u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x512 u32x128x2 bool u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32x128x24 u32 -> u32x128x512
s add p8 p1
@opr a p2 s
o call shrwo p3 p2 p5 p6 p1 p7
ok at o 0
ov at o 1
k select p4 ok a_k
v select p4 ov a_v
isn eq k 1
isr eq k 9
oc call shoc v p9 p10 p11
ca sub p9 1
rc add ca v
ci0 select isn oc rc
act or isn isr
ci1 select act ci0 3071
@rd np p12 ci1
nk select act 1 k
nv select act np v
@rd cnt p0 5
d mul p13 5
base add 8 d
a2 mul cnt 2
o2 add base a2
@wr w0 p0 o2 nk
o3 add o2 1
@wr w1 w0 o3 nv
cnt1 add cnt 1
@wr w2 w1 5 cnt1
ret w2
end
fn shrwe u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32x128x2 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32x128x24 u32x128x24 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
# p0 IM p1 c p2 nodes p3 args p4 nt p5 inf p6 first node p7 ci p8 pi p9 R p10 kind p11 caf
# p12 nra p13 LV p14 RK p15 g p16 rect p17 cty p18 n'
@rd live p13 p1
lv eq live 1
ca sub p7 1
ge ge p1 ca
cr add ca p9
lt2 lt p1 cr
isrepl and ge lt2
cltca lt p1 ca
cpi ge p1 p8
dpi select cpi 1 0
jlo add p1 dpi
jhi0 sub p1 p9
jhi add jhi0 2
jold select cltca jlo jhi
g add p6 jold
@nrow n p2 g
@rd nty p4 g
r sub p1 ca
is3 eq p10 3
r0 eq r 0
r1 eq r 1
rop3 select r1 20 27
rop30 select r0 23 rop3
rop select is3 rop30 20
rna3 select r1 p12 2
rna select is3 rna3 p12
rce3 select r1 p15 0
rcef select is3 rce3 p15
rty3 select r1 p16 p17
rty30 select r0 p16 rty3
rty select is3 rty30 p17
op select isrepl rop n_op
na select isrepl rna n_na
ce select isrepl rcef n_ce
pd select isrepl 0 n_pd
ty select isrepl rty nty
@rd pos p14 p1
d mul pos 5
t add 8 d
@wrs w0 p0 t op lv
t1 add t 1
@wrs w1 w0 t1 na lv
t2 add t 2
@wrs w2 w1 t2 ce lv
t3 add t 3
@wrs w3 w2 t3 pd lv
t4 add t 4
@wrs w4 w3 t4 ty lv
cn select lv na 0
r2 fold shrwe1 cn w4 p3 p5 isrepl p10 r p11 n_af p7 p8 p9 p14 p18
ret r2
end
fn shrw u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x45 u32x128x24 u32x128x2 u32 bool -> u32x128x512
@bodyd d p2 p5
@rd ci p4 5
@rd pi p4 6
@rd kind p4 1
@rd cty p4 8
@rd nra p4 4
@rd gidx p4 11
@rd rect p4 3
is3 eq kind 3
rr select is3 3 1
t1 add d_n rr
mm sub t1 2
mg select p6 mm 0
gc add d_f ci
@nwd caf p0 gc 3
@retop rt p1 d_rw
z call zcol
isn eq rt_k 1
oc0 call shoc rt_v ci pi rr
ix select isn oc0 3071
@wrs lv0 z ix 1 isn
lv fold shrwl mg lv0 p0 p1 p4 d_f mm ci pi rr kind caf nra
z2 call zcol
rk0 rec z2 0
rkr fold shrwr mg rk0 lv
rk at rkr 0
np at rkr 1
im0 call z512
@wr h1 im0 1 np
imf fold shrwe mg h1 p0 p1 p3 p4 d_f ci pi rr kind caf nra lv rk gidx rect cty np
@rd pairs imf 5
@rd rpos rk oc0
rk1 select isn 1 rt_k
rv1 select isn rpos rt_v
@wr h2 imf 2 rk1
@wr h3 h2 3 rv1
d5 mul np 5
b8 add 8 d5
room0 sub 65536 b8
room shr room0 1
over gt pairs room
cd select over 4 0
@wr h4 h3 0 cd
ret h4
end
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# fuseLoops: up to 8 rounds of fuseOnce on function f. A round finds a site (shfsearch), builds
# the fused body, installs it as a new function at the end of the tables, cleans it up, and
# rewrites f (in place when the new body fits the old rows, else at the end).

fn shsum1 u32 u32 u32x128x128 u32 -> u32
g add p3 p1
@nwd na p2 g 2
r add p0 na
ret r
end
# the operand pairs of function f = p2 (and 1 for a ret literal slot)
fn shsum u32x128x128 u32x128x45 u32 -> u32
@bodyd d p1 p2
t fold shsum1 d_n 0 p0 d_f
k shr d_rw 28
k5 eq k 5
x select k5 1 0
r add t x
ret r
end

#@template shround
sr%NAME% call shfsearch nodes%Q% args%Q% fns%Q% ty%Q% tl%Q% nt%Q% p6 p7 rsn
fd%NAME% at sr%NAME% 0
bl%NAME% at sr%NAME% 1
in%NAME% at sr%NAME% 2
ms%NAME% at sr%NAME% 3
fdx%NAME% ne fd%NAME% 0
stp1%NAME% ne lim%Q% 0
stp2%NAME% ne mis%Q% 4294967295
stp%NAME% or stp1%NAME% stp2%NAME%
nstp%NAME% select stp%NAME% false true
go%NAME% and fdx%NAME% nstp%NAME%
gon%NAME% select go%NAME% 1 0
@rd kd%NAME% in%NAME% 1
@rd s2%NAME% in%NAME% 10
is3%NAME% eq kd%NAME% 3
g3%NAME% and go%NAME% is3%NAME%
tr%NAME% call shtyrec ty%Q% tl%Q% nty%Q% ntl%Q% s2%NAME% g3%NAME%
ty%NAME% at tr%NAME% 0
tlr%NAME% at tr%NAME% 1
rt%NAME% at tr%NAME% 2
nty%NAME% at tr%NAME% 3
ntlr%NAME% at tr%NAME% 4
@rd rv%NAME% bl%NAME% 4
rm6%NAME% mul rv%NAME% 6
rr%NAME% add rm6%NAME% 20
@wrs bp%NAME% bl%NAME% rr%NAME% rt%NAME% g3%NAME%
@wrs i3%NAME% in%NAME% 3 rt%NAME% g3%NAME%
@wrs i16%NAME% i3%NAME% 16 rt%NAME% g3%NAME%
@wr i11%NAME% i16%NAME% 11 nf%Q%
ima%NAME% call shb2im bp%NAME%
@rd imn%NAME% ima%NAME% 1
@rd imp%NAME% ima%NAME% 5
@rd imrv%NAME% ima%NAME% 3
@rd npar%NAME% i11%NAME% 2
@rd res%NAME% i11%NAME% 3
nodesa%NAME% call shinn nodes%Q% ima%NAME% nn%Q% na%Q% go%NAME%
argsa%NAME% call shina args%Q% ima%NAME% na%Q% go%NAME%
nta%NAME% call shint nt%Q% ima%NAME% nn%Q% go%NAME%
tla%NAME% call shinl tlr%NAME% i11%NAME% ntlr%NAME% go%NAME%
fnsa%NAME% call shinf fns%Q% nf%Q% ima%NAME% ntlr%NAME% npar%NAME% res%NAME% nn%Q% na%Q% go%NAME%
bigx%NAME% ge imrv%NAME% 268435456
bigxn%NAME% select bigx%NAME% 1 0
imns%NAME% select go%NAME% imn%NAME% 0
impa%NAME% add imp%NAME% bigxn%NAME%
impas%NAME% select go%NAME% impa%NAME% 0
npars%NAME% select go%NAME% npar%NAME% 0
nnx%NAME% add nn%Q% imns%NAME%
nax%NAME% add na%Q% impas%NAME%
nfx%NAME% add nf%Q% gon%NAME%
ntlx%NAME% add ntlr%NAME% npars%NAME%
gz%NAME% select go%NAME% nf%Q% nfx%NAME%
imb%NAME% call ozopt1 ty%NAME% tla%NAME% fnsa%NAME% nodesa%NAME% nta%NAME% argsa%NAME% gz%NAME% nty%NAME% nfx%NAME% nax%NAME%
@rd bcode%NAME% imb%NAME% 0
@rd bmis%NAME% imb%NAME% 7
bok%NAME% eq bcode%NAME% 0
go1%NAME% and go%NAME% bok%NAME%
nodesb%NAME% call shinn nodesa%NAME% imb%NAME% nnx%NAME% nax%NAME% go1%NAME%
argsb%NAME% call shina argsa%NAME% imb%NAME% nax%NAME% go1%NAME%
ntb%NAME% call shint nta%NAME% imb%NAME% nnx%NAME% go1%NAME%
fnsb%NAME% call shinf3 fnsa%NAME% nf%Q% imb%NAME% nnx%NAME% nax%NAME% go1%NAME%
@rd imbn%NAME% imb%NAME% 1
@rd imbp%NAME% imb%NAME% 5
@rd imbrv%NAME% imb%NAME% 3
bigy%NAME% ge imbrv%NAME% 268435456
bigyn%NAME% select bigy%NAME% 1 0
imbns%NAME% select go1%NAME% imbn%NAME% 0
impb%NAME% add imbp%NAME% bigyn%NAME%
impbs%NAME% select go1%NAME% impb%NAME% 0
nny%NAME% add nnx%NAME% imbns%NAME%
nay%NAME% add nax%NAME% impbs%NAME%
imf%NAME% call shrw nodesb%NAME% argsb%NAME% fnsb%NAME% ntb%NAME% i11%NAME% p7 go1%NAME%
@rd fcode%NAME% imf%NAME% 0
@rd fn%NAME% imf%NAME% 1
@rd fp%NAME% imf%NAME% 5
@rd frv%NAME% imf%NAME% 3
@bodyd df%NAME% fnsb%NAME% p7
@nwd s0%NAME% nodesb%NAME% df%NAME%_f 3
tot%NAME% call shsum nodesb%NAME% fnsb%NAME% p7
dk%NAME% shr df%NAME%_rw 28
dk5%NAME% eq dk%NAME% 5
dk5n%NAME% select dk5%NAME% 1 0
avail%NAME% add tot%NAME% dk5n%NAME%
bigz%NAME% ge frv%NAME% 268435456
bigzn%NAME% select bigz%NAME% 1 0
need%NAME% add fp%NAME% bigzn%NAME%
fitn%NAME% le fn%NAME% df%NAME%_n
fita%NAME% le need%NAME% avail%NAME%
inpl%NAME% and fitn%NAME% fita%NAME%
ok0%NAME% eq fcode%NAME% 0
go2%NAME% and go1%NAME% ok0%NAME%
nd%NAME% select inpl%NAME% df%NAME%_f nny%NAME%
ad%NAME% select inpl%NAME% s0%NAME% nay%NAME%
nodesc%NAME% call shinn nodesb%NAME% imf%NAME% nd%NAME% ad%NAME% go2%NAME%
argsc%NAME% call shina argsb%NAME% imf%NAME% ad%NAME% go2%NAME%
ntc%NAME% call shint ntb%NAME% imf%NAME% nd%NAME% go2%NAME%
fnsc%NAME% call shinf2 fnsb%NAME% p7 imf%NAME% nd%NAME% ad%NAME% go2%NAME%
nfn%NAME% select inpl%NAME% 0 fn%NAME%
nfns%NAME% select go2%NAME% nfn%NAME% 0
needn%NAME% select inpl%NAME% 0 need%NAME%
needns%NAME% select go2%NAME% needn%NAME% 0
nn%NAME% add nny%NAME% nfns%NAME%
na%NAME% add nay%NAME% needns%NAME%
nf%NAME% mov nfx%NAME%
ntl%NAME% mov ntlx%NAME%
bad1%NAME% gt nn%NAME% 2730
bad2%NAME% gt na%NAME% 32768
bad3%NAME% gt nf%NAME% 822
bad4%NAME% gt ntl%NAME% 8320
bad5%NAME% gt nty%NAME% 8320
bad6%NAME% ne fcode%NAME% 0
bb1%NAME% or bad1%NAME% bad2%NAME%
bb2%NAME% or bb1%NAME% bad3%NAME%
bb3%NAME% or bb2%NAME% bad4%NAME%
bb4%NAME% or bb3%NAME% bad5%NAME%
bb5%NAME% or bb4%NAME% bad6%NAME%
bb0%NAME% and go1%NAME% bb5%NAME%
bl4%NAME% eq bcode%NAME% 4
bl4g%NAME% and go%NAME% bl4%NAME%
bb%NAME% or bb0%NAME% bl4g%NAME%
limn%NAME% select bb%NAME% 1 0
lim%NAME% or lim%Q% limn%NAME%
nfd%NAME% eq fd%NAME% 0
nmn%NAME% ne ms%NAME% 4294967295
mq%NAME% eq mis%Q% 4294967295
mm1%NAME% and nfd%NAME% nmn%NAME%
mm2%NAME% and mm1%NAME% mq%NAME%
mis1%NAME% select mm2%NAME% ms%NAME% mis%Q%
bm7%NAME% eq bcode%NAME% 7
bm7g%NAME% and go%NAME% bm7%NAME%
mq2%NAME% eq mis1%NAME% 4294967295
bm7h%NAME% and bm7g%NAME% mq2%NAME%
mis%NAME% select bm7h%NAME% bmis%NAME% mis1%NAME%
cnt%NAME% add cnt%Q% gon%NAME%
tl%NAME% mov tla%NAME%
fns%NAME% mov fnsc%NAME%
nodes%NAME% mov nodesc%NAME%
args%NAME% mov argsc%NAME%
nt%NAME% mov ntc%NAME%
#@end

# fuseLoops of function p7 under recordState p8 (p6 the shape table, whose scalars hold the
# counts): (status, missing, function count, ty, tl, fns, nodes, ntys) or, as shfargs, the
# operands. status 0 nothing fuses, 1 fused, 4 a table is full, 7 a body is needed (missing).
#@template shpipe
fn %NAME% u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x45 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32x128x200 u32 bool -> %RET%
@rd nn0 p6 25472
@rd na0 p6 25473
@rd nf0 p6 25474
@rd nty0 p6 25475
@rd ntl0 p6 25476
ty0 mov p0
tl0 mov p1
fns0 mov p2
nodes0 mov p3
args0 mov p4
nt0 mov p5
cnt0 mov 0
mis0 mov 4294967295
lim0 mov 0
rsn select p8 1 0
@inst shround a1 Q=0
@inst shround a2 Q=a1
@inst shround a3 Q=a2
@inst shround a4 Q=a3
@inst shround a5 Q=a4
@inst shround a6 Q=a5
@inst shround a7 Q=a6
@inst shround a8 Q=a7
?mne ne misa8 4294967295
?pos gt cnta8 0
?st1 select pos 1 0
?st2 select mne 7 st1
?limb ne lima8 0
?st select limb 4 st2
?r rec st misa8 nfa8 tya8 tla8 fnsa8 nodesa8 nta8
?ret r
!ret argsa8
end
#@end
@inst shpipe shfuse NEST=1 RET=(u32,u32,u32,u32x384x65,u32x128x65,u32x128x45,u32x128x128,u32x128x24)
@inst shpipe shfargs NEST=0 RET=u32x128x512
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Entries around fusion.

# the counts of the chunk's tables (the free node, operand pair, function, type and tlist
# positions) into the shape table: fusion appends from there
fn shcounts u32x128x200 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x200
@wr a p0 25472 p1
@wr b a 25473 p2
@wr c b 25474 p3
@wr d c 25475 p4
@wr e d 25476 p5
ret e
end
# is there a fusion site in function f = p7? (found, a body that is needed and absent or 4294967295)
fn shfcheck u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x45 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32x128x200 u32 bool -> (u32,u32)
rsn select p8 1 0
sr call shfsearch p3 p4 p2 p0 p1 p5 p6 p7 rsn
fd at sr 0
ms at sr 3
r rec fd ms
ret r
end
# the shape columns of the fused function f and of the synthetic functions nf0 .. nf1 - 1 of the
# fused tables: SYN 1 for a synthetic body, 2 for f, FUSED[f] = f + 1
fn shfsh1 u32x128x200 u32 u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x45 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32 -> u32x128x200
g add p8 p1
r call shpass p0 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 g
@colw s1 r 15104 g 1
ret s1
end
fn shfsh u32x128x200 u32x384x65 u32x128x65 u32x128x45 u32x128x128 u32x128x512 u32x128x24 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x200
n sub p9 p8
a fold shfsh1 n p0 p1 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p8
b call shpass a p1 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p7
@colw c b 15104 p7 2
f1 add p7 1
@colw d c 14080 p7 f1
ret d
end
